{
  "schema": 1,
  "meta": {
    "name": "ship",
    "description": "Cut the pending work as one release - changelog then release in a single command"
  },
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "id": "pk-ship",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "pk ship"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Runs "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "pk changelog"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " then "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "pk release"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " as one invocation. "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "pk ship"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " carries no state of its own: what remains is the "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "Release-Tag"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " trailer on HEAD and whether its tag exists. A run interrupted between the halves resumes at release on rerun."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "id": "usage",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Usage"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "codeblock",
      "lang": "bash",
      "text": "pk ship --dry-run\npk ship\n"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "--dry-run"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " previews the section when nothing is pending, or rehearses the release when a Release-Tag commit exists; the release half cannot be rehearsed before its changelog commit exists."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "If the release half fails, the changelog commit stands. Rerun "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "pk ship"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " to retry, or "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "pk changelog --undo"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " to unwind."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "id": "deciding-the-version",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Deciding the version"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The commits decide the version. "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "pk ship --dry-run"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " shows the bump they infer, and that bump is the release. A version named earlier, in a plan or in the conversation, was a guess made before the commits existed; it is never a target to make the release match. When the inferred version is not the one that was expected, stop and say so, with the commits that set it. A commit whose type is wrong, a "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "feat"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " that is really a "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "fix"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " or a "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "chore"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", is fixed by amending that commit's type before shipping, while it is unpushed; the bump then follows."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "--bump"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " and "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "--exclude"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " are the developer's, and pass through to changelog. "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "--bump"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " is for the case the commits cannot show, when the developer knows the inferred bump is wrong for a reason outside the messages. "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "--exclude"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " leaves commits out of the section, which is the developer's call in the same way. Use either only when the developer asks for it, with the exact value given."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "codeblock",
      "lang": "bash",
      "text": "pk ship --bump patch       # only when the developer asked for patch\n"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "guard asks before a "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "--bump"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " lower than the commits infer, patch over a "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "feat"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " or minor over a breaking change, and lists the commits that call for the higher bump; see "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "pk help guard"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", Version bumps. The changelog half names an override next to the version it generates."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "id": "releasing",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Releasing"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Releasing is the developer's call. Run "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "pk ship"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " when the developer asks for a release, not on your own reading of a preview. When the inferred bump is a major, show the commits carrying "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "!"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " or "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "BREAKING CHANGE"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " and the section, and wait for the developer's go."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "id": "flags",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Flags"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "codeblock",
      "text": "  --bump \u003cvalue\u003e\n        Override the inferred bump: major, minor, or patch (the developer's call; passed to changelog)\n  --dry-run\n        Rehearse: preview the section, or the release when one is already pending\n  --exclude \u003cvalue\u003e\n        Comma-separated commit SHAs to drop from the section (the developer's call; passed to changelog)\n"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Every command also accepts "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "--plain"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "--project-dir \u003cvalue\u003e"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", and "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "--quiet"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "; see "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "pk help help"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
